NOTICE
================================================================================

This work — the Undal platform, comprising its specification corpus, source code,
brand assets, audio assets, build workflows, and documentation — is licensed under
the Public Availability with Source Code Visibility License, Version 1.0 ("PASVL-1.0").

The canonical, controlling text of PASVL-1.0 and of the Letter of Software
Deployment Approval ("LOSDA") instrument is published at:

    https://github.com/bsdc-info-bd/PASVL_LOSDA

In the event of any divergence between this notice and the canonical text, the
canonical text governs.

================================================================================
WHAT THIS MEANS IN PRACTICE
================================================================================

SOURCE IS PUBLIC.
    You may read, study, audit, fork, and learn from every line of this repository.
    The source code is deliberately visible. Security researchers, students, and
    prospective partners are invited to inspect it.

DEPLOYMENT REQUIRES A LOSDA.
    Running this software as a service — operating it for yourself, for an
    organisation, or for the public; serving orders; taking payment; dispatching
    riders — requires a Letter of Software Deployment Approval issued by the
    rights holder. Reading the code does not grant the right to run it.

ATTRIBUTION IS MANDATORY.
    Every source file in this repository carries, and must continue to carry, the
    license header reproduced below.

================================================================================
REQUIRED FILE HEADER
================================================================================

Every source file, workflow file, and specification document in this repository
carries the following header, in the comment syntax appropriate to the file type:

    Licensed under PASVL-1.0. Source is public. Deployment requires a LOSDA.
    SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-PASVL-1.0

Continuous integration enforces the presence of this header. A pull request that
adds a file without it will not pass the `license-headers` job.

================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
================================================================================

Undal depends on third-party software distributed under its own terms. Those terms
are not superseded by PASVL-1.0, and the obligations they impose are independent
of, and additional to, the obligations in this file. The principal components and
their licenses are enumerated in `docs/39-risk-register-and-truths.md`, Section 11,
and reproduced in machine-readable form in `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md` once the build
begins.

Map data rendered by Undal is © OpenStreetMap contributors and is made available
under the Open Database License (ODbL). Every surface in Undal that renders OSM
tiles — the customer app, the partner app, the rider app, the web storefront, and
the administrative command map — displays the required attribution. Removing that
attribution is both a license violation and a failing CI check
(`osm-attribution` job, see `docs/28-cicd-github-actions.md`, Section 14).

